<ResourceDictionary
    x:Class="FeWoLearning.Uno.Exercises.Advanced.Ex086_DesignTokens"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        TODO: Ex086 - build a two-layer token system.

        ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries with "Light" and "Dark", each declaring the
        *primitive* tokens:
          * SolidColorBrush "SurfaceBrush" - White in Light, Black in Dark
          * x:Double "SpacingUnit" - 4 in Light, 8 in Dark (a stand-in for a density
            change; real systems vary spacing by platform rather than by theme, but the
            mechanism is the same)

        Then, outside the theme dictionaries, the *semantic* layer: a base Style for Border
        keyed "CardBaseStyle" setting Background to {ThemeResource SurfaceBrush} and Padding
        to 4, and a Style keyed "CardCompactStyle" that is BasedOn CardBaseStyle and
        overrides Padding to 2.

        Two layers is the whole idea: primitives change per theme, semantics stay put, and
        a consumer names only the semantic style. Note that a Style cannot live inside a
        theme dictionary and be BasedOn one outside it - which is why the split is this way
        round.
    -->

</ResourceDictionary>
